-- Script:  universe-content-pt-duplication.sql
-- Purpose: One-time historical duplication — creates a Portuguese row for every
--          existing English content row (characters, lore, eras, archetypes,
--          signs), joined to its English counterpart by translation_group_id.
--          Companion data migration to keynor-core PR #64 (schema/backend) and
--          PR #65 (Aroneus/Siegmund workflow docs). Character names are
--          preserved verbatim (never translated); lore/era/archetype/sign names
--          are translated. 'valkani' and 'dohundred' are kept as-is in all PT
--          text per the universe glossary (aniannoth-overview/.claude/
--          universe-glossary.md) — they are never rendered in Portuguese.
--          Translations by Lethra; structured into this script by Aroneus/
--          Siegmund. Source text for characters/lore was read directly from
--          the live database, not from db/seed/universe-content.sql — that
--          file's character/lore bodies are stale/truncated (see the PR
--          description for this finding, reported separately to Imaws).
-- Target:  eras, map_eras, archetypes, signs, characters, character_categories,
--          lore, lore_categories, universe_entity_images, entity_links
-- Effect:  266 new rows inserted (52 eras, 1 map_era, 5 archetypes, 13 signs,
--          18 characters, 18 character_categories, 9 lore, 11 lore_categories,
--          47 universe_entity_images, 92 entity_links). No existing EN row is
--          modified, updated, or deleted — this script is purely additive.
-- Author:  Siegmund (Level 2 — keynor-core)
-- Date:    2026-07-10
--
-- PREREQUISITE: migrations V13/V14 (language + translation_group_id columns)
-- must already be applied and run — this script will fail against a database
-- that does not yet have those columns.
--
-- AUTHORIZATION REQUIRED before this runs — it is a bulk INSERT (protected action).

